id: pm-fhifkc
title: "Two of the three ci-triggered assurance gates never ran on a pull request, so the append-only history assertion that carries the immutability guarantee was evaluated only after merge"
description: "Three gates declare the trigger ci in the assurance registry: tracker-context-quality with 40 assertions, graph-composition with 7, and record-integrity with 1. Only the first was wired into the pull-request workflow.\n\nMeasured 2026-08-13. ci.yml ran a single assurance invocation, tracker-context-quality, under the static matrix leg. graph-composition and record-integrity reached a runner only through pnpm quality:static, which appears in nightly.yml and release.yml and in no pull-request path. So both gates declared themselves ci-triggered and neither was evaluated by CI in the sense that matters, which is before a change merges.\n\nThe one that matters most is record-integrity, whose single assertion is history-append-only at block enforcement. That assertion is the machine-checkable form of the guarantee the product is built around: every mutation permanently recorded, the record not alterable afterwards, any version restorable. A change that violated it would pass every pull-request check, merge, and be caught that night at the earliest — after it was already in the immutable record, which is the one place where after is materially different from before.\n\ngraph-composition is less severe and the same shape: seven assertions on edge composition and semantic share, evaluated nightly against a main branch that already contains whatever changed them.\n\nThis is not a gap in the declarations. The registry is correct, the triggers are correct, all three gates pass today, and the assertions are well formed with negative controls. The gap is entirely in the wiring, which is exactly the class pm-cu1i and its relatives keep producing: a capability declares where it should run and nothing checks that it runs there. The general remedy is that the gate registry should derive workflow wiring from the declared triggers rather than have a human keep two lists in agreement, which is what pm-1jzupz's premise implies and what gate-registry.mjs already half does by discovering gates through a regex over workflow step names."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[6]: assurance,ci,governance,history,immutability,merge-safety
created_at: "2026-08-13T14:37:01.915Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-13T14:39:58.770Z"
