comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-13T14:39:46.138Z","harness:claude-code","Evidence: ci.yml step 'Run tracker context-quality ratchets' replaced by 'Run tracker assurance gates', which now runs all three ci-triggered gates on the static matrix leg — tracker-context-quality, graph-composition and record-integrity.\n\nVerified locally on the same tree: all three return verdict pass under --trigger ci --dry-run --json, and scripts/release/gate-registry.mjs still reports ok with registered_gate_count 12 and enforced_pipeline_count 18, so renaming the step did not break gate discovery.\n\nScope note for the residual: this change makes the wiring correct today and does not make it self-checking. The equivalence between the set of gates declaring the ci trigger and the set wired into the pull-request workflow is still maintained by hand, which is the recurrence risk the description names. That half stays open on this item's acceptance criteria and belongs with pm-1jzupz, whose premise is that enforcement is declared data rather than duplicated lists."
